 180          // System UART Command: drains the UART receive buffer, builds lines,
 181          // handles CLI commands (help, clear, IP dump, MAC set).
 182          // Bytes that belong to a JSON data line ('{' ... newline) are never
 183          // treated as CLI commands.
 184          // FIX: a '{' ALWAYS starts a new JSON line (buffer is reset), so a lost
 185          // newline or stray byte can no longer let JSON letters trigger the CLI.
 186          void sys_uart_cmd(void)
 187          {
